ine which produces mica insulating washer for use in electric device to turn out washer having a thickness of 10 mm. A sample of 10 washers has an average thickness 9.52 mm with a standard deviation of 0.6 mm. Find out t-score. (Upto 3 decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"-2.528","high":"-2.528"},"solution":"<p>-2.528</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/eaf109653929dfeb03699610e0884c8f79b5b23d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":29,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following statements are correct?<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>1</sub> : The t-distribution is used when the population standard deviation is known and sample size is large.<br />\n<em>S</em><sub>2</sub> : The degree of freedom for t-distribution depend on the sample mean.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n Only <em>S</em><sub>1</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n Only <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n Both <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> and <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n Neither <em>S</em><sub>1</sub> nor <em>S</em><sub>2</sub></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":30,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>X</em> is a Poisson random variable, such that 2<em>P</em>(<em>X</em> = 0) = <em>P</em>(<em>X</em> = 1), the standard deviation of the distribution is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 1</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/5515ba87f9531c09c6d9f492686311168da4dfe5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 2</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 4</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/03261333d112cf65304b1803fd8d050b9bfc4173.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":31,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>In a single throw with two dice, the probability that the sum is a perfect square is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/0fb953518f66fbafb808d20f230d7b775b4fa90a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/1b32006449872a9c5e28d0861507c182b23c657a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/f2e58d2f3df752b57a3bac83ded79d1f987242cd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <p>\n <img src=\"/media/3ed27257490e9c06f21dd954120a1f9e4c55175f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/23528366aa08c388ed2f82730ded9324bb68aadd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":32,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Number of tigers in a reserve is normally distributed with mean and variance respectively as 1200 and 9 × 10<sup>4</sup>. The probability of finding more than 1800 tiger is approx.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 0.0125</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 0.025</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 0.05</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> None of these</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/32ca27425c222c33d389f392abb4a0737fef6bd0.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/14864e3ca63c8e9cfed78269990c60e1438bd747.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":33,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>Let <em>X</em> be a continuous random variable with following probability density function.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/fbf78e0eca535c